From 7de04d6bf0e9a4047ccf8985d74fdcf4f771b7b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): shield Engram row cache from prefill floods and
 support pinned scales

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 4652b632a3c6bf5f65da7d2bfb750b203e671aa2.

Rationale:
1. In _row_plan.h, the 65,536-row 4-way set-associative host Engram row cache previously used pure FIFO replacement (advancing set->clock on every cache miss without recording hits or distinguishing large prefill chunks from decode steps). After 0750 enabled the row cache across all batch sizes, a 32K-64K chunked prefill (8-16 chunks of 4,096 tokens = 262,144-524,288 owned lookups on TP3, 4x-8x the cache capacity) streams one-time prompt n-grams through all four ways of every cache set, evicting the active decode working set and causing interleaved prefill_yield and post-prefill decode steps to suffer cold NVMe misses.
2. Add 2-bit saturating usage counters (uint8_t usage[4] + uint8_t reserved[3] placed in the existing 7-byte struct padding after uint8_t clock in ple_cache_set_t, keeping sizeof(ple_cache_set_t) at 1,096 bytes while 8-byte aligning weights and scales) and prefill probationary insertion:
   - Promote set->usage[w] up to PLE_CACHE_MAX_USAGE (3) on cache hits in ple_plan() and on duplicate in-step hits in ple_cache_insert().
   - Classify each ple_plan() pass as a prefill chunk when its live rank-owned column lookups exceed PLE_CACHE_MAX_TOKENS (64 tokens) and it is not an explicit background prefetch. Because serve() plans step.early and reader->late separately, mixed prefill+decode steps treat the early prompt chunk as probationary and the late decode tokens as protected decode rows.
   - On cache misses in ple_cache_insert(), fill empty ways (ids[w] < 0) first and existing probationary ways (usage[w] == 0) second. When all four ways hold protected rows (usage >= 1), prefill misses (is_prefill) claim at most one single-touch way (usage == 1) per set as a probationary slot (usage = 0) without aging the remaining three ways and never evict multi-hit ways (usage >= 2), while decode/verify misses (!is_prefill) sweep set->clock with 2-bit Clock decay until a way reaches zero.
3. Add opt-in two-plane scale pinning (SPARK_DS41F_ENGRAM_PIN_SCALES=1 or EngramDiskRows(..., pin_scales=True)) so two-plane mode can preload the 8-byte-per-row scale shard into host memory via pread + POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED and serve scale bytes on cache misses without issuing a second 4 KiB O_DIRECT io_uring read per miss.

Quality:
Bit-exact (torch.equal) with the baseline packed and two-plane disk Engram readers across all batch sizes and sharding modes.

Tests:
- pytest --noconftest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_engram_rows.py (52 passed across 2 boots), including test_row_cache_clock_pro_prefill_shield_preserves_decode_working_set and test_two_plane_pinned_scales_halves_read_calls_and_matches_reference.

Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 disk Engram optimization.
